course: dictionary
lesson: 14799
title: Punishable
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Punishable is an adjective. It tells you that something can be punished, which means the people in charge can give a penalty for it.
explain: Look at the word parts: punish and able. Able means can be, so punishable means can be punished. «Stealing is a punishable offence.» An offence is a wrong act, so stealing is wrong, and the law can give a penalty for it.
explain: Signs and rules often use this word. «Dropping litter is punishable by a fine.» The words after «punishable by» tell you the penalty: here it is a fine, which means you have to pay money.
fact: Punishable means something that can be punished by law or by rules.
fact: Punishable is often used in rules, laws and safety signs.
fact: «Punishable by» is followed by the penalty, such as «punishable by a fine».
fact: «Punishable offence» means a wrong act that has a penalty.
fact: The opposite of punishable is allowed, which means there is no penalty.
exercise: «Stealing is a punishable offence.» What does punishable mean here? | Something that is easy to find | Something that is very old | Something that makes you laugh | *Something that can be punished by law or rules
exercise: The sign says «Dropping litter is punishable by a fine.» What kind of punishment is it? | A trip to the park | *A fine, which means you pay money | A warning to say sorry | A prize for a tidy street
exercise: Which word means the opposite of punishable? | *Allowed | Dangerous | Broken | Expensive
test: «Speeding on the road is punishable by law.» What does punishable by law mean? | *It can be punished by the law | It has been taken off the list | It is a kind rule for children | It is a rule about cooking food
test: The rule says «Being rude to others is a punishable offence.» What is punishable here? | The word rude itself | The teacher who makes the rules | *The wrong act, which can be punished | The friend who was rude
exam: «Cheating in a test is a punishable offence, so the school can give a penalty.» What does punishable mean in this sentence? | Something that is fun to do | Something that the school has to give out as a prize | *Something that can be punished, so there is a penalty | Something that is easy to hide
